From fbc5bb53c049899a75f3db97c33fccc7bf796698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sfermigier@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:48:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] brand: drop the ONLYOFFICE favicon

favicon.ico is ONLYOFFICE's stacked-sheets device -- the trademark itself,
not a wordmark -- and the same file five times over. It is the last piece of
their artwork that reaches a built payload: everything else is either written
over by the theme (the About and header logos in apps/common/main) or lives
under a directory build/dist.sh does not ship.

Deleted rather than replaced. The page it belongs to is loaded in a webview
with no tab, no bookmark bar and no history entry, so there is nowhere for a
favicon to appear; the application icon is the host's job and is set from the
desktop entry, the bundle, or at runtime. The <link> goes with it, in all
twenty-one pages that carry one, source and .deploy alike -- leaving it would
turn a shipped trademark into a shipped 404.

The theme mechanism cannot reach these. deploy-theme-images.js writes to
apps/common/{main,mobile} and apps/<editor>/mobile only; nothing it does lands
in apps/<editor>/main/resources/img/, which is where these are.

This patch is not for upstream.
